questionAnswers.Q5:
Census and closure soundness are unchanged; the round-6 model diff touches only boot-entry rules.
Refused:
- S-a, S-d, S-f, S-g and S-e;
- I-a, with a consistent image;
- C-a, C-b, C-c and C-e;
- W4-b.
I found no way for a bundle to carry its own observation of a foreign cgroup, process or program and qualify. No role can run another role's code or an interpreter's.
The stated residuals stand: interpreted scripts are declared, not observed; a Python runtime outside the tree; a fabricated unpopulated census entry with a matching count.

questionAnswers.Q6:
My independent replay rebuilds every case from fresh JSON copies. Each case gives exactly its pinned result:
- the 4 positives are accepted under full, v1-only, v2-only and attested-empty histories, and refused 'test-only implementation profile' without the fixture flag;
- 207/207 negatives, including 52 schema-level refusals, each a single error;
- 9/9 accepted variants;
- 14/14 cross-version cases;
- 14/14 migration cases.
Single-defect status changed in round 6 (R6-3(a)):
- V67, V71 and V72 are single-defect: each is accepted when only its own rule is disabled;
- V42 is double-defect, as stated;
- every one-sided command-line negative also breaks the binding.
The positives are byte-identical to round 5 and remain plausible for the kernel and the loader. A08 and A09 are plausible. A09's PARTUUID=8c4f2a10-01 has the MBR form, which is valid on an MBR-partitioned ESP.

extraProbes.observed:
Caught by an accept/refuse change:
- '+', UUID-only and PARTUUID (A09);
- rw, quiet and loglevel= (A08);
- dropping initrd=, root=UUID|PARTUUID|LABEL, ro, security=, selinux=, enforcing= or lockdown= from the grammar (the positives);
- count >= 1 (V67);
- binding dropped (V71, V72).
Caught by a message change only, because the one-sided negatives also break the binding (R6-3(a)): '--', 'any word', systemd.*, SYSTEMD_*, rd.*, runlevel digits, --unit, rootflags=, console=, the unit allowed in ENROLLED, lockdown in either entry, match or search instead of fullmatch (V75, V69, V70, V63), selinux=[0-9] (V73) and enforcing=[0-9] (V74).
Uncaught:
- re-admitting rootfstype=;
- any initrd= value;
- any root=, root=/dev/ or LABEL= form;
- loglevel=[0-9]+, lockdown=[a-z]+ and security=[a-z]+;
- order-insensitive, set-based, superset, root=/initrd=-only and unit-last bindings (R6-3(b) and (c));
- splitting on whitespace runs, which is benign because the kernel and systemd also coalesce spaces.

